@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+## Why
+
+A task is only known by its title, so anything that refers to a task breaks when it is renamed. The app needs a stable reference that survives renames.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets an `id`: a string no other task of the list has, kept for the task's whole life (including renames).
+- `add` returns the task with its `id`.
+- The list gets `get(id)`, returning the task with that id as a `Result`, like the other methods.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-identity`: tasks have a unique, stable id, and the list can look up and act on a task by id.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts` (`Task`, `createTask`), `src/domain/list.ts` (`TaskList`, `createTaskList`), `test/list.test.ts` (the task shape now includes `id`).
+- Public API in `src/index.ts` is unchanged apart from the extended types.
+- No new dependency.
